## Try to load shader from files and bind default locations.
## @param vs_file_name Optional vertex-shader file path. null requests the native default. Present text must be NUL-free UTF-8.
## @param fs_file_name Optional fragment-shader file path. null requests the native default. Present text must be NUL-free UTF-8.
## Native lifetime, thread, input-extent and required device/context checks retain their checked failures.
## @return Ok with one shader owner to release using unload_shader; Err(load_error) if no owner is acquired or resource validation fails. Rejected temporary owners are released. Both null arguments intentionally request the default and may succeed; otherwise a wholly default program is Err(default_fallback). A nondefault program does not prove every requested stage was used.
func try_load_shader(vs_file_name: c_string?, fs_file_name: c_string?) -> result<shader, load_error>:
    return _try_shader(load_shader(vs_file_name, fs_file_name), "load_shader", vs_file_name == null and fs_file_name == null)

## Try to load shader from code strings and bind default locations.
## @param vs_code Optional vertex-shader source code. null requests the native default. Present text must be NUL-free UTF-8.
